     "photosynthesis",
     "chlorophyll",
     "transpiration"
    ],
    "text": {
     "en": "Leaves make food by photosynthesis using sunlight, water and carbon dioxide. They give out oxygen.\nPlants lose water as vapour from leaves through tiny pores in a process called transpiration. This pulls water up from the roots.\nChlorophyll gives leaves the green colour and helps trap sunlight."
    }
